    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0558" n="546" xml:id="pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20/247</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Iranian Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shayesteh</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Honorable the Minister of
                    Iran and refers to the Legation’s note of September 20, 1943 requesting the
                    assignment of additional personnel to the United States Military Mission at
                    Teheran.</p>
                <p>The War Department has informed the Department of State that the United States
                    Army is deployed on a world-wide front against the common enemy and that the
                    need for Army personnel is such that the number so assigned to Iran must be kept
                    to the minimum capable of providing the advice and assistance requested and
                    utilized by the Iranian Government. The War Department has also stated that
                    before a request for an increase in the size of the Mission would be considered
                    it would have to have the approval of Major General C. S. Ridley, Chief of the
                    Mission, and when approved it would still be necessary for the War Department to
                    weigh the request against the many demands for officer personnel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-19">October 19,
                            1943</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
